LStudio After Hours
===================

The default hightechmess app is now a BPM-based club lighting playground.
Run `pnpm --filter @projects/hightechmess start` and open http://127.0.0.1:3210.
Six scenes, editable16-step rhythms, four-color palettes, MIDI draft controls,
saved sessions and synchronized onboard playback for up to four OctaCore towers.
Send & play uses the connected compatible towers; absent towers are optional.
Tower IDs 1 and 2 retain compatibility with the current left/right boards.

See docs/CONTROLS.md and docs/RUNBOOK.md. Old frame streaming remains available
with start:legacy for recovery; it is no longer the default.

# lstudio

MIDI Mix lighting controller for two OctaCore ESP32 boards:

- Left: `ws://octacore-left.local:81` (virtual strip 0)
- Right: `ws://octacore-right.local:81` (virtual strip 1)

The four-strip virtual model remains intact for existing presets. Only the first
two strips are transmitted. Servo commands are disabled in the active output.
MIDI mappings and per-preset brightness behavior are retained.

See [the local runbook](docs/RUNBOOK.md) for installation, hardware-free checks,
startup, IP overrides, and recovery. Wi-Fi credentials belong in the paired
OctaCore firmware's private configuration, not in this repository.
